      <!-- Methodology -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display mb-3" style="font-size:1.5rem;color:#F2EEE5;font-weight:600;">How the 12-month numbers were built</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">The starting point was the vendor's own published pricing page. Where a vendor obscures the real monthly bill behind "custom quote" or per-calendar scaling, the numbers were cross-checked against third-party pricing teardowns written by competitors and consultants (Gymdesk, GlossGenius, Pabau, StudioStackPro). Payment processing was added using the rates each vendor actually charges, applied against a revenue assumption for each business size. The add-ons that wellness customers commonly end up buying (branded app, SMS reminders, email marketing, website builder) were included, because leaving them out produces a number the studio owner does not recognize.</p>
        <p>The resulting 12-month total was conservative: it used the low end of each range and the published floor price rather than aggregator estimates of the real quote, and it left out setup fees and contract-renewal price hikes (which several vendors routinely charge).</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Vendor pricing sources -->
      <div>
